events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/corngood/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Sure, this was just to align with the xdg spec.\r\n\r\nIf we keep this as `get_data_path`, I'm a bit worried that `get_data_dirs` will be confusing, because it doesn't actually include the 'home' path.\r\n\r\nI think my best idea for a name is `get_data_search_paths`, and I think it would be best to include `get_data_path()` in the list.  So you have `get_data_path` for a single, writable data dir, and `get_data_search_paths` when you want to search for something that may be in a non-writable location.\r\n\r\nAlso, just for my curiosity, are the compatibility concerns because of the script interface, or the C++ interface?  I assume we could alias the script function if we had to?","created_at":"2025-05-05T18:51:53Z","updated_at":"2025-05-05T18:51:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105836#discussion_r2073992835","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105836","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2073992835"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105836#discussion_r2073992835"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105836"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2073992835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":288,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2062679453,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2083302805","pull_request_review_id":2831076939,"id":2083302805,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc58LK2V","diff_hunk":"@@ -285,7 +285,8 @@ class OS {\n \tString get_safe_dir